Find the perimeter of a parallelogram with sides $14\text{ cm}$ and $9\text{ cm}$. Its internal perpendicular height is $7\text{ cm}$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=3mm,y=3mm,draw=black,text=black,line width=0.5pt,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,0)--(14,0)--(19.657,7)--(5.657,7)--cycle;
\draw[dashed] (5.657,0)--(5.657,7);
\draw (5.657,0.7)--(6.357,0.7)--(6.357,0);
\path (7,0) node[below] {$14\text{ cm}$};
\path (16.829,3.5) node[right] {$9\text{ cm}$};
\path (5.657,3.5) node[left] {$7\text{ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Find the perimeter of this rhombus. Its internal diagonal is $6\text{ cm}$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=3mm,y=3mm,draw=black,text=black,line width=0.5pt,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,0)--(7.416,3)--(14.832,0)--(7.416,-3)--cycle;
\draw[dashed] (7.416,-3)--(7.416,3);
\draw (3.558,1.871)--(3.858,1.129);
\draw (10.974,1.129)--(11.274,1.871);
\draw (10.974,-1.129)--(11.274,-1.871);
\draw (3.558,-1.871)--(3.858,-1.129);
\path (11.124,1.5) node[above right] {$8\text{ cm}$};
\path (7.416,0) node[right,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] {$6\text{ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
